  "cautions": [
    "Each printed-table label is a singer-oriented editorial IPA proposal, not a phonemic or measured acoustic transcription.",
    "The first-tranche parsing of y and w reflects written Pinyin conventions and does not guarantee a direct final-row IPA realization.",
    "Written i includes sibilant-conditioned apical values beyond the explicit retroflex-i row in the dissertation; no automatic value is assigned.",
    "Written o, ong, u, uan, and un can require initial-dependent normalization or source-table variants, and additional spellings may likewise require context.",
    "Written iu, ui, and ue are linked to the full-form source headings iou, uei, and üe rather than presumed identical IPA letters.",
    "No candidate source table option is automatically selected as the IPA for any real first-tranche syllable.",
    "The source geometric symbol registry remains an arbitrary written-letter code; 27 complex finals still lack a full constructed articulatory-feature candidate."
  ]
